    "explanation": "1. CONCEPT:\nSynthesis of linear silicone polymers.\n\n2. GIVEN:\n(CH3)2SiCl2 + 2H2O -> (CH3)2Si(OH)2 + 2HCl.\n\n3. FORMULA / PRINCIPLE:\nBifunctional dimethylsilanediol condenses head-to-tail to produce straight-chain polydimethylsiloxanes.\n\n4. STEP-BY-STEP SOLUTION:\n1. Dimethyldichlorosilane (CH3)2SiCl2 has two hydrolyzable chlorine atoms.\n2. Hydrolysis yields dimethylsilanediol (CH3)2Si(OH)2, which is bifunctional.\n3. Intermolecular condensation of these diols yields long linear chains of repeating -[Si(CH3)2-O]- units.\n\n5. FINAL ANSWER:\nOption A: (CH3)2SiCl2\n\n6. WHY OTHER OPTIONS ARE WRONG:\nCH3SiCl3 is trifunctional and produces cross-linked polymers; (CH3)3SiCl is monofunctional and terminates chains.",
