    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "1. CONCEPT:\nHess's Law application to carbon allotrope transition.\n\n2. GIVEN:\nC(graphite) + O2 -> CO2 (Delta H = -393.5 kJ/mol); C(diamond) + O2 -> CO2 (Delta H = -395.4 kJ/mol).\n\n3. FORMULA / PRINCIPLE:\nDelta H_transition = Delta H_comb(graphite) - Delta H_comb(diamond) = -393.5 - (-395.4) = +1.9 kJ/mol.\n\n4. STEP-BY-STEP SOLUTION:\n1. Subtracting the combustion equation of diamond from graphite:\n2. C(graphite) -> C(diamond).\n3. Delta H = (-393.5) - (-395.4) = +1.9 kJ/mol.\n4. The positive value indicates that diamond has higher enthalpy than graphite and is an endothermic transition.\n\n5. FINAL ANSWER:\nOption A: +1.9 kJ/mol\n\n6. WHY OTHER OPTIONS ARE WRONG:\nDiamond is higher in energy by 1.9 kJ/mol, confirming graphite is the thermodynamically favored allotrope.",
