    "explanation": "1. CONCEPT:\nRefining of nickel by Mond process and carbonyl bonding.\n\n2. GIVEN:\nNi + 4CO -> [Ni(CO)4] (330-350 K) -> Ni + 4CO (450-470 K).\n\n3. FORMULA / PRINCIPLE:\nCO is a neutral ligand, giving oxidation state 0 and coordination number 4 (sp3 tetrahedral).\n\n4. STEP-BY-STEP SOLUTION:\n1. Carbon monoxide is a neutral ligand with charge 0.\n2. In [Ni(CO)4], nickel has an oxidation state of 0.\n3. Four CO molecules donate pairs of electrons, giving a coordination number of 4.\n4. The geometry is tetrahedral (sp3 hybridization).\n\n5. FINAL ANSWER:\nOption A: 0 and 4\n\n6. WHY OTHER OPTIONS ARE WRONG:\nOxidation state is 0 because CO is neutral.",
